WEBVTT

00:08.300 --> 00:15.500
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:08.300 --> 00:15.500
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

00:15.540 --> 00:22.250
Setsunai hodo mune utsu kagirinai kibou

00:15.540 --> 00:22.250
This unbounded hope that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

00:23.050 --> 00:30.850
Hakanasa wo masu hibi wo
irodoru wa kisetsu no kaze

00:23.050 --> 00:30.850
The days pass by, becoming more fleeting,
colored by the season's wind

00:30.890 --> 00:35.560
Kioku no kakera ga sawagidashita yo

00:30.890 --> 00:35.560
The fragments of memory started running wild

00:36.160 --> 00:44.560
Arinomama wo mitomete
haruka tsumuida hikari ga

00:36.160 --> 00:44.560
One more time, I want to hold the
spindle of far off light close to my breast,

00:44.610 --> 00:52.240
Kieru mae ni mou ichido
kono mune ni dakishimete

00:44.610 --> 00:52.240
Before it disappears, before
I accept the way things are now

00:54.320 --> 01:01.520
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:54.320 --> 01:01.520
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

01:01.520 --> 01:08.660
Mirai wo egaku ao ni kono te wo nobashite

01:01.520 --> 01:08.660
Hold out this hand to the blue-painted future

01:08.830 --> 01:15.960
Kasokushiteku sekai yo douka
yasashii mama de ite

01:08.830 --> 01:15.960
The world accelerates, please let it stay this kind

01:16.070 --> 01:23.570
Setsunai hodo mune utsu afuredasu negai

01:16.070 --> 01:23.570
This overflowing wish that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

01:32.320 --> 01:37.450
That was how I met a spirit of nature,
called a "Djinn".

01:38.930 --> 01:45.030
And I experienced their sense of perception.

01:46.700 --> 01:53.770
I wonder if the sun is always
watching over us all like this?

02:04.820 --> 02:07.260
That's plenty!

02:07.260 --> 02:08.820
Thanks, Ichika.

02:08.820 --> 02:10.850
Just keep doing it like this.

02:11.190 --> 02:13.060
Roger...

02:15.130 --> 02:20.330
You've got to return that charm from
a special someone back to normal, right?

02:22.440 --> 02:25.110
Yes, you're right...

02:25.110 --> 02:29.610
So that's how I ended up having to use
the Djinn's power another 11 times.

02:31.450 --> 02:34.250
What other kinds of Djinn are there?

02:35.250 --> 02:38.590
Y-you don't want me to spoil the surprise, right?

02:38.590 --> 02:41.720
Wait, could it be you don't know
yourself, Manatsu?

02:45.800 --> 02:50.300
The Neighboring Night Sky

02:56.470 --> 02:57.870
It's bright...

02:57.870 --> 02:59.670
It's morning, Manatsu!

03:02.980 --> 03:05.610
What? It's still so early...

03:05.610 --> 03:07.340
No, it's not.

03:09.450 --> 03:11.040
Here's a change of clothes.

03:14.860 --> 03:16.920
We're going to do radio exercises!

03:16.930 --> 03:20.190
Aw, sheesh! I'm so not a morning person.

03:20.200 --> 03:22.250
Ichika, good morning!

03:22.800 --> 03:24.770
Oh, it's Hiro and Niwa!

03:24.770 --> 03:26.670
Good morning!

03:26.670 --> 03:30.810
You still come to exercises
even though you're a second year?

03:30.810 --> 03:32.570
And why shouldn't I?

03:32.570 --> 03:35.070
Everyone else always quits coming.

03:46.190 --> 03:47.160
Ichika!

03:48.020 --> 03:49.420
Maki!

03:49.420 --> 03:50.320
Later.

03:50.330 --> 03:51.380
Sure, bye!

03:53.730 --> 03:57.630
It's been a while!
You're still doing radio exercises?

03:57.630 --> 03:59.000
You always got up early.

03:59.000 --> 04:00.400
And what about you, Maki?

04:02.240 --> 04:05.470
I pulled an all-nighter.

04:05.470 --> 04:07.640
She didn't sleep a wink all night.

04:09.340 --> 04:10.640
Who are you?

04:12.580 --> 04:15.070
Maki's friend, right?

04:15.580 --> 04:17.150
Stop it, Ryou.

04:17.150 --> 04:19.020
Ichika, who's that girl?

04:21.460 --> 04:24.360
I'm Manatsu, Ichika's pen pal!

04:24.360 --> 04:25.520
Nice to meet you!

04:26.190 --> 04:27.460
It's starting!

04:28.030 --> 04:32.970
Good morning! Let's do radio exercises
and get energized!

04:35.040 --> 04:36.870
A pen pal?

04:36.870 --> 04:40.570
But I thought you didn't do
email and stuff, Ichika?

04:41.180 --> 04:42.080
Um...

04:42.080 --> 04:44.480
Since you live close by, she can just call you.

04:44.480 --> 04:46.040
My house is really far away, see!

04:47.020 --> 04:50.080
So's mine! Tell me your email address...

04:51.190 --> 04:55.620
Ichika, don't go telling strangers
you just met your email, got it?

04:56.260 --> 04:58.190
It's okay, Manatsu.

04:58.190 --> 04:59.420
I'm sorry.

05:02.060 --> 05:02.790
Here.

05:06.030 --> 05:09.500
He's your friend, right?

05:09.500 --> 05:10.700
I guess so.

05:11.110 --> 05:12.470
All set. Thank you.

05:13.110 --> 05:14.910
Later Ryou, I'm going home.

05:14.910 --> 05:17.480
Wait, Maki? Maki!

05:17.480 --> 05:18.950
Another time then...

05:19.710 --> 05:20.880
Maki!

05:27.090 --> 05:30.250
I am so not a morning person!

05:33.630 --> 05:34.620
Ichika...

05:36.100 --> 05:39.470
Don't you regret telling him your email?

05:39.470 --> 05:41.630
No, I don't...

05:48.240 --> 05:49.540
Good morning!

05:49.850 --> 05:50.710
Good morning.

05:55.120 --> 05:57.080
Isn't she pretty?

05:57.090 --> 06:00.350
Her name is Saya, and she lives next door.

06:04.730 --> 06:07.920
I hear she works in the fashion industry.

06:11.470 --> 06:13.260
We're back!

06:26.310 --> 06:27.050
Hello!

06:27.050 --> 06:27.920
Pardon us.

06:27.920 --> 06:30.510
Good day. Ichika is in her room.

06:31.590 --> 06:33.520
It's Sei and Kai!

06:34.790 --> 06:36.120
What am I going to do?

06:36.120 --> 06:39.920
I can't let Sei see the charm
with the colors changed!

06:41.530 --> 06:42.690
C-coming!

06:46.300 --> 06:49.840
So, let's set up a schedule for the summer.

06:49.840 --> 06:50.410
Yes!

06:50.410 --> 06:53.240
Oh, you're really rarin' to go, Ichika!

06:53.240 --> 06:55.040
Yeah, no kidding!

06:55.040 --> 06:58.580
This town's got the ocean, and the mountains...

06:58.580 --> 07:00.210
There's a ton of places to have fun!

07:00.580 --> 07:02.610
No way I'll be bored!

07:03.690 --> 07:05.090
What?

07:05.090 --> 07:06.780
It's boring since you live here?

07:08.160 --> 07:10.450
Sei, Kai...

07:10.790 --> 07:12.430
Let me introduce you.

07:12.430 --> 07:17.130
This is my pen pal who is staying over
during summer vacation, Manatsu.

07:17.470 --> 07:18.660
Nicetameetcha!

07:19.330 --> 07:23.830
Manatsu, these are my two home tutors, Sei...

07:24.540 --> 07:26.140
Nice to meet you, Manatsu.

07:26.140 --> 07:27.410
...and Kai.

07:27.410 --> 07:28.140
Yo.

07:29.010 --> 07:31.150
Home tutors?

07:31.150 --> 07:34.720
So that means the special person
you got that from is...

07:34.720 --> 07:35.710
"That?"

07:42.290 --> 07:44.520
It was a number of days earlier...

07:45.590 --> 07:49.360
It was surely just a little...

07:49.360 --> 07:50.990
Just a small coincidence.

07:58.010 --> 07:59.600
It's been six years.

08:00.740 --> 08:04.700
It's now the right time to be set free
from this spell.

08:05.910 --> 08:07.510
Don't you think so, Kai?

08:08.680 --> 08:10.380
I've said it before.

08:10.390 --> 08:12.440
You didn't do anything wrong.

08:12.750 --> 08:13.780
The person to blame is...

08:14.760 --> 08:15.380
Who's there?!

08:17.230 --> 08:18.660
I-I'm
sorry!

08:20.460 --> 08:21.860
Oh, it's you, Ichika!

08:21.860 --> 08:23.630
You don't have to apologize.

08:23.630 --> 08:24.890
Coming home from school?

08:25.830 --> 08:26.800
Yes!

08:26.800 --> 08:28.570
I saw the two of you, and...

08:29.240 --> 08:31.760
What are you doing?

08:32.340 --> 08:36.400
I was thinking of burying something
with a lot of memories.

08:36.850 --> 08:39.550
Like a time capsule, or something.

08:39.550 --> 08:41.070
I see...

08:41.750 --> 08:44.650
It must be important to you.

08:55.300 --> 08:55.820
Do you want it?

08:56.130 --> 08:58.700
Oh, I don't...

08:58.700 --> 09:00.570
Why don't I give it to you, Ichika?

09:02.840 --> 09:04.310
Are you sure?

09:04.310 --> 09:04.770
Yes.

09:14.180 --> 09:15.980
Thank you very much!

09:15.980 --> 09:18.180
I'll treasure it, I promise!

09:19.720 --> 09:24.660
But I had already broken that promise.

09:25.230 --> 09:26.890
Because at that time,

09:26.900 --> 09:32.390
the color of the stones had been changed
by the mysterious power of the Djinn.

09:33.770 --> 09:36.640
Manatsu, please keep that a secret.

09:36.640 --> 09:37.660
What?

09:38.270 --> 09:40.510
Oh, sure thing.

09:40.510 --> 09:42.680
Two girls telling each other secrets?

09:42.680 --> 09:44.310
Can't help but be curious.

09:44.310 --> 09:45.750
Please, don't worry about it!

09:45.750 --> 09:46.710
That's right!

09:46.710 --> 09:49.050
Secrets are one of a woman's charms!

09:49.050 --> 09:49.540
Isn't that right?

09:50.450 --> 09:51.980
That may be true.

10:06.730 --> 10:11.230
So you see, since I'd like
to show Manatsu around,

10:11.540 --> 10:15.270
I'll use the library to study on my own...

10:15.840 --> 10:16.900
On your own?

10:17.650 --> 10:22.150
I'm sorry. I know Ichika should be
studying more over the summer, but...

10:22.880 --> 10:23.780
No, it's okay.

10:23.790 --> 10:27.810
We'll start tomorrow and trade off
on our usual schedule.

10:28.190 --> 10:29.520
I'm sorry...

10:30.230 --> 10:31.560
What is it?

10:31.560 --> 10:35.160
Oh, I figured I would go to the library right away.

10:35.160 --> 10:35.930
Work hard.

10:36.200 --> 10:37.030
I will!

10:43.340 --> 10:45.310
This is so boring!

10:45.310 --> 10:47.240
Sheesh, Manatsu!

10:49.240 --> 10:51.580
I hate quiet places!

10:51.580 --> 10:53.240
Manatsu...

10:58.790 --> 10:59.720
Thank you.

11:01.190 --> 11:05.190
But man, there go our summer plans.

11:05.190 --> 11:06.290
Yes, indeed.

11:06.830 --> 11:10.990
You didn't go on your club's training camp
because of the tutoring, right?

11:11.670 --> 11:16.800
Well, I'm not sure if Ichika will study on her own,
but I can train on my own!

11:17.640 --> 11:18.610
Good luck with that!

11:21.410 --> 11:23.540
But looking at those two...

11:23.550 --> 11:24.770
It brings back memories.

11:25.380 --> 11:27.370
Of that summer...

11:30.490 --> 11:32.450
Yeah, it does...

11:48.570 --> 11:51.870
Ichika, you're such a stickler.

11:54.380 --> 11:55.180
That's hot!

11:55.180 --> 11:56.040
Hot, hot, hot!

11:57.550 --> 12:00.740
I hope Manatsu is okay by herself.

12:05.950 --> 12:07.390


12:07.390 --> 12:08.490
Ryou?

12:08.490 --> 12:10.890


12:10.890 --> 12:13.290
That person I met this morning?

12:24.070 --> 12:25.230
Now that's just mean.

12:27.780 --> 12:31.110
I was passing by here and noticed you...

12:31.110 --> 12:34.810
So I sent you an email. Pretty cold of you, man.

12:43.520 --> 12:45.460
Ichika, you okay?

12:45.460 --> 12:47.830
I saw him go inside, so...

12:47.830 --> 12:48.990
Manatsu...

12:51.100 --> 12:54.340
Well, I'm sorry if I surprised you!

12:54.340 --> 12:56.340
I treated you so cut me some slack.

12:56.340 --> 12:59.770
You think you can buy us off with a Popsicle?

12:59.770 --> 13:01.640
Oh, Manatsu...

13:01.640 --> 13:06.080
Yeah, but isn't it bad manners since
I went to the trouble of mailing you?

13:07.050 --> 13:08.350
I'm sorry!

13:08.850 --> 13:12.250
I just really wanted to finish up
my homework first.

13:12.550 --> 13:15.720
You choose homework over your friends?

13:15.720 --> 13:17.290
You're her pen pal, right Manatsu?

13:17.290 --> 13:18.430
What do you think?

13:18.430 --> 13:20.490
I think it depends on the person.

13:20.500 --> 13:22.020
Oh hush, Manatsu!

13:23.300 --> 13:27.930
A single, tiny lie will beget falsehoods
one after another.

13:29.240 --> 13:32.640
And from that chain, no one can escape.

13:33.840 --> 13:38.210
So while I often swapped emails with Manatsu,

13:38.210 --> 13:41.280
it was really more like correspondence.

13:41.280 --> 13:42.780
Sort of like an exchange diary,

13:42.780 --> 13:47.190
I'd send her mails about what I did that day...

13:47.190 --> 13:48.620
Things like that.

13:48.890 --> 13:52.850
It became a habit to mail her after it got dark.

13:55.030 --> 13:57.260
Is something the matter?

13:57.270 --> 14:00.930
You're actually pretty talkative, Ichika.

14:01.340 --> 14:03.330
That's not true...

14:04.770 --> 14:06.930
I hated lies.

14:07.580 --> 14:11.210
Those who are taken in by lies,
and those who tell lies...

14:11.710 --> 14:15.880
And me, for lying to myself.

14:17.620 --> 14:21.920
I can't let Sei see the charm
when the colors have changed!

14:21.920 --> 14:25.390
I'd like to use the library to study on my own...

14:25.390 --> 14:26.830
I'm sorry!

14:26.830 --> 14:29.890
I just really wanted to finish up
my homework first.

14:30.800 --> 14:34.200
I've been lying all the time lately.

14:34.200 --> 14:35.400
What's the matter, Ichika?

14:37.410 --> 14:39.770
I'm going home.

14:40.340 --> 14:42.740
Thank you for the ice cream bar.

14:45.850 --> 14:47.840
Hey, don't leave so soon!

14:48.780 --> 14:51.250
Nobody likes pushy guys!

14:52.020 --> 14:53.180
Wait!

14:56.060 --> 14:57.530
I won't let you go home.

14:57.530 --> 14:59.730
I need something from you.

14:59.730 --> 15:00.790
Ichika!

15:03.930 --> 15:04.920
I said wait!

15:10.240 --> 15:11.940
Ichika, faster!

15:11.940 --> 15:15.200
Hold it! I'm not going to do anything, it's just...

15:19.910 --> 15:21.250
That's enough already!

15:26.790 --> 15:28.090
That's...

15:33.190 --> 15:35.730
Hello? This is Sanae.

15:35.730 --> 15:37.260
I just saw Ryou...

15:37.270 --> 15:39.700
This is the opposite direction from my house!

15:40.330 --> 15:42.600
So you want to lead him to your house?

15:42.600 --> 15:43.970
That's not...

16:01.990 --> 16:04.650
Wait! I just want to...

16:07.060 --> 16:08.890
I said wait!

16:13.570 --> 16:14.560
Ichika!

16:19.040 --> 16:19.840
Ryou!

16:21.480 --> 16:22.500
Maki...

16:24.010 --> 16:25.780
What are you doing with Ichika?

16:25.780 --> 16:27.110
Maki...

16:27.480 --> 16:29.250
Nothing.

16:30.550 --> 16:32.450
I'm being punished.

16:33.020 --> 16:35.850
Because I didn't tell the truth...

16:36.290 --> 16:38.730
Because I told lies...

16:38.730 --> 16:40.060
This is my punishment.

16:41.230 --> 16:43.100
Nothing my ass.

16:44.270 --> 16:46.930
Ichika sure is cute.

16:46.930 --> 16:49.340
And that Manatsu chick ain't bad herself.

16:49.340 --> 16:51.710
I've got homework to do. I'm going home.

16:51.710 --> 16:52.510
Goodbye.

16:52.510 --> 16:53.840
Hey, Maki!

16:53.840 --> 16:55.370
Wait, Maki!

16:58.950 --> 17:00.780
Idiot... Suit yourself.

17:06.220 --> 17:07.210
Hey!

17:09.090 --> 17:10.620
Maki, why you...

17:10.630 --> 17:12.250
Never show your face to me again.

17:12.930 --> 17:14.360
Screw you!

17:14.700 --> 17:15.820
Somebody help!

17:16.500 --> 17:19.700
Scream all you want!
Nobody's going to come out here!

17:19.700 --> 17:21.070
Run, Ichika!

17:26.910 --> 17:28.980
It's said that the light of the moon

17:28.980 --> 17:31.880
has led people astray since long ago, however...

17:31.880 --> 17:35.710
That's nothing but shifting
the blame to others, yes?

17:38.590 --> 17:41.060
Anyway, I have to call someone!

17:41.060 --> 17:42.150
Ichika, look!

17:47.360 --> 17:50.630
Please, Djinn... Lend me your power!

18:34.240 --> 18:36.140
The power of the Moon Djinn, Luna...

18:38.880 --> 18:39.470
What's that?

18:40.510 --> 18:41.710
Bright, isn't it?

18:42.020 --> 18:44.050
Ichika turned on that light!

18:44.050 --> 18:47.350
Her voice might not reach,
but people will come to that light!

18:48.260 --> 18:50.280
As if!

18:58.300 --> 19:01.140
Sorry for showing up at such a cliché time.

19:01.140 --> 19:02.240
Kai!

19:02.240 --> 19:03.070
Yo.

19:03.070 --> 19:04.700
Why, you...

19:08.310 --> 19:13.110
Sorry. If I did that during a match
I'd get suspended.

19:14.450 --> 19:15.510
Ryou!

19:21.690 --> 19:23.460
Damn you!

19:23.460 --> 19:25.150
Good for you, Ryou.

19:25.690 --> 19:28.630
Looks like she really does love you.

19:34.570 --> 19:35.500
Maki...

19:48.720 --> 19:51.920
Don't get other people mixed up
in your lover's quarrels anymore!

19:51.920 --> 19:53.250
Got it, playboy?

19:56.160 --> 19:59.460
Game over. You can come out now.

19:59.930 --> 20:02.130
Ichika's clothes were ripped.

20:02.130 --> 20:03.960
She doesn't want to show herself to you, Kai.

20:05.700 --> 20:06.800
Are you okay?

20:06.800 --> 20:07.500
Yes!

20:07.500 --> 20:08.900
I am... okay.

20:10.000 --> 20:11.870
Okay, then we'll be going now.

20:13.670 --> 20:15.040
I'll take you home!

20:15.040 --> 20:17.940
And I'll lend you my jersey, so...

20:19.850 --> 20:22.910
Well, they sure are fast.

20:28.360 --> 20:30.190
Sei, it's me.

20:30.690 --> 20:31.920
Stay quiet and listen.

20:32.490 --> 20:35.620
I didn't think it was really possible... But...

20:39.200 --> 20:40.970
Let's go home.

20:40.970 --> 20:41.560
Okay!

20:52.850 --> 20:55.250
You're angry, aren't you?

20:56.650 --> 21:00.420
When I thought, maybe
we could start over again,

21:00.420 --> 21:02.950
I wanted to ask Ichika...

21:10.230 --> 21:11.360
Thank goodness.

21:11.670 --> 21:12.500
Huh?

21:12.930 --> 21:14.700
It's nothing.

21:14.700 --> 21:16.970
I was just thinking, "how nice."

21:19.810 --> 21:21.340
Yes.

21:21.340 --> 21:26.470
Back then I simply thought to myself "how nice."

21:43.060 --> 21:45.430
That makes two.

21:47.430 --> 21:50.400


21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
Hora kotoshi mo ame furu gogo
hakanai utakata no iro

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
See, this year the afternoon rain falls again
in the color of fleeting bubbles

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
Sora mo yasashiku mienai wa
datte hitori da mono

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
The sky doesn't look kind to me, after all,
I'm alone

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
Itazura na sadame ni kotoba mo denai wa

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
I have no more words for the tricks of fate

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Wakariaeta futari ni mou modorenai no?

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Can we never return to two
who understood each other?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

23:20.390 --> 23:21.700


23:21.700 --> 23:24.630
After being separated far apart...

23:25.000 --> 23:27.500
Being able to be close to one another,
to have personal contact...

23:27.500 --> 23:32.840
On that day I came to realize
the pleasure hidden within.

23:34.200 --> 23:39.200
On the next Uta~Kata:
The Heat of the Sandy Beach
